1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,538
Your company uses artificial
intelligence to read CVs,

5
00:00:04,588 --> 00:00:08,501
answer customers and make
small decisions every day.

9
00:00:09,573 --> 00:00:12,846
But if one day someone asks
you: “What exactly did it do,

13
00:00:12,896 --> 00:00:15,592
and how can you prove it?”, could you answer?

17
00:00:19,267 --> 00:00:24,630
This is sigillo. Every action your AI
takes is recorded in a way that nobody,

21
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:29,252
not even whoever runs the system,
can change without it showing.

25
00:00:33,401 --> 00:00:39,254
Connecting your agent takes a few minutes. Give
your system a name, and sigillo gives you its key.

29
00:00:42,824 --> 00:00:48,145
Drop in your agent's file. Sigillo reads it
in your browser and tells you what it found.

33
00:00:48,195 --> 00:00:50,133
Nothing is sent anywhere.

37
00:00:54,560 --> 00:01:00,324
Download the file: it comes back with sigillo
already in it. Replace your own file with it.

41
00:01:03,383 --> 00:01:07,875
Run your agent as usual. A moment
later the first receipt arrives,

45
00:01:07,925 --> 00:01:10,845
and every action it takes is on record.

49
00:01:15,333 --> 00:01:19,785
On the right, an agent screening
applications for a developer job.

53
00:01:26,634 --> 00:01:30,632
With every CV, the ledger on
the left updates by itself.

57
00:01:36,485 --> 00:01:40,977
And at the top, the answer to the first
question: all good, no tampering.

61
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:55,142
The history, in plain sentences: what the
agent did, when, and how it turned out.

65
00:01:56,797 --> 00:02:01,688
The technical details are there, but they
stay out of sight until you look for them.

69
00:02:04,123 --> 00:02:08,403
Every action has its own fingerprint,
linked to the one before it:

73
00:02:08,453 --> 00:02:12,011
none can vanish or change
without breaking the chain.

77
00:02:15,035 --> 00:02:18,173
And you can look at just the tools the agent used.

81
00:02:20,667 --> 00:02:27,245
Several times a day the ledger is sealed, and an
external, independent authority adds its timestamp.

85
00:02:31,954 --> 00:02:38,019
It proves those actions already existed at
that time: nobody can rewrite them afterwards.

89
00:02:43,033 --> 00:02:47,110
When an inspector, an auditor or
a customer asks for evidence,

93
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:50,902
one click is enough: sigillo
prepares the evidence pack.

97
00:02:53,433 --> 00:02:59,700
And anyone can check it, with a free, public tool
that does not belong to whoever sells sigillo.

101
00:03:01,570 --> 00:03:04,699
The check passes: the evidence pack is intact.

105
00:03:05,939 --> 00:03:09,131
Now let's change a single character in a copy:

109
00:03:09,181 --> 00:03:13,044
the time of a candidate's
evaluation, moved by one second.

113
00:03:15,582 --> 00:03:18,303
The check fails, and says exactly where.

117
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:24,584
The same goes for documents. A
candidate disputes the selection:

121
00:03:24,634 --> 00:03:28,427
upload their CV. The document
never leaves your computer.

125
00:03:33,273 --> 00:03:38,825
Yes: it is exactly the one the AI read.
Not a similar one: exactly that one.

129
00:03:41,086 --> 00:03:44,946
One different character, and
sigillo no longer recognises it.

133
00:03:48,467 --> 00:03:53,935
The European AI Act asks companies to be
able to show what their systems have done.

137
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:06,322
Sigillo does not tell you whether
your AI did the right thing:

141
00:04:06,372 --> 00:04:09,299
it gives you the evidence to check for yourself.

145
00:04:09,699 --> 00:04:12,661
The pilot is free: get-sigillo.eu.
